-<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/relocating/beaches/#article","headline":"Beach Rules on the Grand Strand, Town by Town","description":"Beach rules across the Grand Strand, town by town: when dogs are allowed, umbrella and tent limits, parking, the winter golf cart season, and who sets each rule.","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/relocating/beaches/","author":{"@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/about/#devin-day"},"reviewedBy":{"@type":"Person","name":"Timothy Nash","alternateName":"Tim Nash","jobTitle":"Broker-in-Charge"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/#org"},"datePublished":"2026-08-27","dateModified":"2026-11-01","inLanguage":"en-US","image":"https://chapter3realty.com/og-image.jpg","mainEntityOfPage":{"@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/relocating/beaches/#webpage"},"about":{"@type":"Thing","name":"Beach Rules on the Grand Strand, Town by Town"},"keywords":"Myrtle Beach beach rules, dogs on beach Myrtle Beach, beach tent rules Myrtle Beach, golf cart on beach"}</script>
-<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/relocating/beaches/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Are dogs allowed on the beach in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. In the City of Myrtle Beach dogs are allowed before 10 a.m. and after 5 p.m. from May 1 through Labor Day, and at any hour the rest of the year, always on a leash of 7 feet or shorter. Each town sets its own clock: North Myrtle Beach allows dogs before 10 a.m. and after 4 p.m. starting May 15, and Pawleys Island allows dogs year round at any hour."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which beach near Myrtle Beach allows dogs all day in summer?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Pawleys Island. The town allows dogs on the beach year round with no daytime ban: leashed 8 a.m. to 8 p.m. from May 1 through September 30, and off leash under voice control, leash in hand, from October through April. Every other beach on the Grand Strand runs a midday summer ban."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are tents allowed on Myrtle Beach beaches?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Depends on the town and the season. Myrtle Beach allows only round umbrellas up to 7.5 feet from Memorial Day through Labor Day, with tents up to 12 by 12 the rest of the year. North Myrtle Beach is umbrella-only May 15 through Labor Day. Surfside Beach allows canopies up to 10 by 10. County beaches like Garden City are umbrella-only all year."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is alcohol allowed on the beach in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Alcohol and glass are prohibited on every beach on the Grand Strand, and on the county beaches the ban covers the access paths too. Fires, including barbecues, are prohibited, and holes deeper than two feet are not allowed in Myrtle Beach; fill any hole before you leave."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you drive a golf cart on the beach in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not in the cities. On Horry County's unincorporated beaches, which include stretches of Garden City, permitted golf carts with a licensed driver are allowed on the sand from November 1 through February 28. That winter season is the exception, not the rule, and the cities do not offer one."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you have to pay to park at the beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Depends where you live and where you park. The City of Myrtle Beach sells no visitor pass but gives its residents a decal covering city paid spaces. North Myrtle Beach posts its rules at each access. Surfside Beach uses town decals. Where you buy decides which program you are in, so pick your town deliberately."}}]}</script>
