+<section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Ohio to Myrtle Beach FAQ</h2><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Is Myrtle Beach cheaper than Ohio?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Mostly, not entirely. You stop paying local income tax, gas costs about 10 cents less, and property tax rates are far lower. Against that, a typical house costs more than in Cleveland, Columbus or Cincinnati, sales tax is higher, and the yearly car tax is new. The calculator on our cost of living page runs your exact city.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Do I pay local income tax in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">No. South Carolina has no city or school district income tax anywhere. Most Ohio cities charge 1 to 3 percent of wages, so for working households this is usually the biggest single change.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">How is retirement income taxed in South Carolina compared with Ohio?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Ohio taxes pensions and retirement account withdrawals with credits that top out at $200 a year. South Carolina allows a deduction instead: up to $15,000 of income per person from age 65, with the retirement income deduction of up to $10,000 counting against that same $15,000. Social Security is untaxed in both.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Does South Carolina tax my car every year?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Yes. Vehicles are taxed yearly on value: a $30,000 car is taxed roughly $360 to $460 plus a $50 road fee, and the bill must be paid before the plate renews. Ohio charges a flat fee of roughly $36 to $74. Add a one-time $250 fee per vehicle when you arrive, within 45 days.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Can Ohio still tax me after I move to South Carolina?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">It can if the move is not clean. Holding an Ohio driver&#39;s license at any point in the year, spending 213 or more nights in Ohio, or missing the October 15 non-residency statement each keep Ohio&#39;s claim alive. The night count does not apply in the year you move. A snowbird split between the two states should bring in a CPA first.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What surprised one of our team most after moving from Ohio?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">The county vehicle bill, which Ohio never sends: every vehicle here is taxed on its value each year. Then two he did not see coming: needing sunglasses daily in summer, and a job market far wider than Pleasant City, the village of about 400 he left.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);margin-top:2.2rem;padding-top:1.5rem;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Who wrote this</p><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;max-width:720px">Chapter 3 Realty is a real estate brokerage in Myrtle Beach, built as a partnership around a simple idea: you should be as informed as possible on the biggest purchase of your life, every single time. Tim Nash is the Broker-in-Charge, South Carolina broker license 43182, with more than 30 years selling real estate on the Grand Strand. He reviews every page we publish and runs our market analyses himself. His father, Fred Nash, also sold real estate here, and Fred Nash Boulevard by Myrtle Beach International Airport is named for him. Devin Day wrote this page. He is our Operations Officer and a relocator himself, from Ohio. Meet the team on <a href="/about/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">the about page</a> or read <a href="/why-chapter-3/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">why buyers work with us</a>. The direct line is <a href="tel:+18543332135" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">854.333.2135</a>.</p></div><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;max-width:720px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://codes.ohio.gov/ohio-revised-code/section-5747.02" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Ohio income tax statute</a>, <a href="https://www.bmv.ohio.gov/doc-fees.aspx" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Ohio BMV fees</a>, <a href="https://codes.ohio.gov/ohio-revised-code/section-5747.24" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Ohio residency statute</a>, <a href="https://dor.sc.gov/news/information-about-h-4216" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none" rel="noopener" target="_blank">South Carolina 2026 income tax</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/tax-payer-services/vehicle-tax/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Horry County vehicle tax</a>. We are not tax advisers; rates change and your situation decides the answer. Verify with a professional before you plan around any of it.</p></div></section>
 
 </div>
 </main>
