;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">January to July 2026</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">3,873</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Same months of 2025</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">4,453</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">July 2026</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">562</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">January to July 2026 is 13.0 percent below the same months of 2025. Most of the permits are single-family houses in planned communities. <a href="/invest/new-construction-rentals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Buying a new house as a rental</a> has the warranty, the incentives and the recorded rules.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is approved and not yet built</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=80af96d3ac864d068045634ac4365405" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The county's planning office keeps a map of every major subdivision</a> with the units its zoning allows and the units built. Subtracting one from the other gives the homes that can still be built without a new approval. On September 8, 2026 that was 44,735 units in the unincorporated county: 29,704 houses and 15,028 apartments or condos. The cities keep their own records.</p><div style="max-width:640px;margin:1rem 0 1.2rem"><svg viewBox="0 0 640 250" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Approved but unbuilt homes by community, unincorporated Horry County" s