rade the area is built on: newer construction and bigger lots than the beach, a short drive from it.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Is Carolina Forest in a flood zone?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Much of it maps outside FEMA's high-risk zones, but pockets of Zone AE exist near ponds and wetlands, so the parcel matters more than the neighborhood. Check any address against the county flood maps in effect since December 16, 2021. Most of Carolina Forest is inland of Carolina Bays Parkway, outside South Carolina's wind pool territory, so wind coverage stays inside a standard homeowner policy. Homes between Carolina Bays Parkway or River Oaks Drive and the Intracoastal Waterway are inside the territory, where a policy can leave wind out.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Can you Airbnb a house in Carolina Forest?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Usually not. Horry County does not prohibit short-term rentals in unincorporated areas, but most Carolina Forest HOAs do: Avalon's recorded rules prohibit any rental under three months, and several communities require one-year minimum leases. Treat it as a long-term rental market and verify the covenants of the specific community before buying for rental income.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What do homes cost in Carolina Forest?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Recent single-family medians are about $418,000 per Redfin's mid-2026 snapshot and $464,710 per SC Realtors data for ZIP 29579 in December 2025, against a roughly $329,000 Horry County median. Condos in the corridor had a median near $215,500. Entry points run from the $200,000s in older condo sections to over $1 million on the Intracoastal.</p></div></div></section>
